lisa-design:
- Scanner: osv-scanner v2.7.0 from its official image, pinned by digest as the Go constant imagescan.ScannerImage (tracked by a renovate.json regex custom manager), run via docker on a `docker save` archive as the runner's uid; offline DBs in ~/.cache/osv-scanner (actions/cache, daily key). Exit 1 = vulns found, 128 = no packages.
- Severity is computed from the advisories' CVSS vectors with pandatix/go-cvss (the library osv-scanner uses), falling back to osv-scanner's group max_severity only when no vector parses. Distro ratings are never used. Actionable = fixed version + score >= 7.0.
- Runtime check: NODE_VERSION env, else `docker run --network none --entrypoint node <img> --version`; OSV API (Bitnami/node), not the offline DB. Fixed = all fixed events > installed; FixedInMajor separates rule-2 cases.
- Rule 1 candidate: X.Y.Z tag -> newest X.Y patch (same suffix, same precision) via registry tag list; else the tag's current digest if the ref pins an older digest; an unpinned floating tag has no candidate (already newest) -> rule 3 note. Candidate must clear ALL actionable findings (sameVuln = same package/source + shared ID/alias).
- Rule 2 trigger: for runtime images (node) only the binary findings; for OS images (debian/alpine) all actionable. Tries supported cycles ascending, keeps the tag suffix. Adds matchCurrentVersion (not in the spec's key list) so the allowedVersions regex doesn't freeze the repo's other node images. Rule 1 is skipped for an image that rule 2 handles (EOL), so automerge true never reaches the major.
- Overrides validation (renovate.ParseOverrides): whitelist keys, exactly one matchRepositories in the run's selection, matchManagers exactly ["dockerfile"], non-empty matchDepNames. Missing/empty file = no overrides.
- renovate.yml: MANIFEST/REPOS/DRY_RUN moved to workflow-level env (shared by the 3 jobs); image-repos computed in select via `image-scan list`; download-artifact continue-on-error; image-scan token Contents read only, dry and live.
- Published images (:main, :latest) are scanned for the report only; their pull failures are notes, not errors. Base image scan failures are errors (exit 1 after outputs are written).

